  "presentation_summary": [
    "38-year-old Sri Lankan woman presented on day 5 of an acute febrile illness with tachycardia and hypotension.",
    "At ward admission she was afebrile but had pulse 120/min and blood pressure 80/60 mmHg, with right-sided pleural effusion, tender hepatomegaly, and free fluid.",
    "Initial blood count showed leukopenia, hemoconcentration, and severe thrombocytopenia with WBC 3400/mm3, hematocrit 49.4%, and platelets 18,000/mm3.",
    "She had acute liver injury and coagulopathy with AST 2450 U/L, ALT 1360 U/L, albumin 2.9 g/dL, PT 19 seconds, and INR 1.58.",
    "She had acute kidney injury with creatinine 4.6 mg/dL and hyperkalemia 5.5 mmol/L, requiring hemodialysis through a femoral venous catheter.",
    "Dengue IgM seroconversion on day 7 of illness supported the dengue diagnosis.",
    "After the dengue shock and organ injury improved, she developed MRSA infective endocarditis and proximal femoral deep vein thrombosis, treated with linezolid and anticoagulation."
  ],
